# Change: Cleanup and Consistency Refactor

## Why

A comprehensive audit of the current codebase against LLM/AI coding principles revealed a small set of concrete issues: a real functional bug (Ctrl+S saves twice), dead build shims with no callers, a stale `project.md` that misleads AI assistants, and repeated `isMac` detection logic with inconsistent APIs. These are targeted fixes — the architecture is already sound and nothing else needs to change.

## What Changes

### High Priority

- **Fix Ctrl+S double-save bug**: `attachGlobalKeyboardShortcuts` (`ui-events.ts:404`) and the editor-local `keydown` listener (`ui-events.ts:195`) both handle Ctrl+S. Without `stopPropagation`, both fire when the editor has focus. Remove the save shortcut from the editor-local handler and rely on the global handler exclusively.

- **Delete dead build shims**: `build/inject.js` (a one-line wrapper around `assemble-single-file.js`) and `build/build.js` (a one-line re-export of `compile-and-assemble.js`) have no npm script references and exist only as backwards-compatibility aliases. Delete both. Update README to remove mentions.

- **Update stale `openspec/project.md`**: The file says "Vanilla JavaScript (ES6+)" and "No formal testing framework currently implemented". The codebase is TypeScript with QUnit + Cypress. AI assistants use this file to understand the project stack — incorrect facts lead to incorrect suggestions.

### Medium Priority

- **Consolidate `isMac` detection into one utility**: Four instances across `ui-events.ts` (lines 192, 263, 394) and `app-controller.ts` (line 140) use two different APIs (`navigator.platform` — deprecated — and `navigator.userAgent` regex). Extract `detectMac(): boolean` into `src/app/utils.ts` and replace all four call sites.

- **Extract export functions from `workspace-io.ts`**: `exportAsJson()` and `exportAsMarkdown()` (lines 711–769) construct `Blob` objects and trigger browser downloads. This has nothing to do with workspace I/O. Move them to a new `src/app/note-export.ts`. This brings `workspace-io.ts` from 834 lines to ~720 and gives each file a single clear responsibility.

- **Add intent comment to mutable-ref pattern in `app-controller.ts`**: `treeHandlers` (lines 49–52) and `rescanWorkspaceRef` (lines 61–63) are initialized as empty stubs then patched later. Without context, AI agents will try to "simplify" this away, breaking initialization. Add a short comment explaining this is a circular dependency workaround.

### Low Priority

- **Replace inline styles in JS string templates**: `workspace-io.ts:807` and `tree-render.ts:126` both contain `style="padding: 8px;"` inside `innerHTML` strings. Extract to a `.tree-empty-state` CSS class in `styles.scss`.

- **Archive completed refactor proposals**: `refactor-align-llm-coding-principles` and `refactor-simplification-plan` are fully checked off but still appear in `openspec list`. Archive both with `openspec archive`.

### Keep As-Is (No Change Needed)

- `workspace-io.ts` overall structure — cohesive except for export functions; no further splitting needed.
- `tree-render.ts`, `cogito.ts`, `types.ts`, `tags.ts` — already clean, right-sized.
- Factory function and dependency injection patterns throughout — already well structured.
- Test coverage (QUnit + Cypress) — keep and expand around touched areas only.
- `build/inject.js` and `build/build.js` export names are not public API — deletion has no external breakage risk.

## Impact

- Affected specs: `codebase-maintainability`
- Affected code:
  - `src/app/ui-events.ts` (remove duplicate Ctrl+S handler; replace isMac calls)
  - `src/app/app-controller.ts` (replace isMac call; add comment to mutable refs)
  - `src/app/utils.ts` (add `detectMac` utility)
  - `src/app/workspace-io.ts` (remove export functions)
  - `src/app/note-export.ts` (new file — extracted export functions)
  - `src/styles.scss` (add `.tree-empty-state` class)
  - `build/inject.js` (delete)
  - `build/build.js` (delete)
  - `openspec/project.md` (update tech stack facts)
  - `README.md` (remove references to deleted build shims)
</file>

